############################################################
### PART B: negative cases for the new proactive checks ###
############################################################
--- B1. RecordShipment to an unknown destination org -- expect rejection ---
(setup RegisterComponent + RecordTest AUTH2-NEG-SHIP as OEM, both committed VALID)
Error: endorsement failure during invoke. response: status:500 message:"recordShipment rejected: toOrg \"NotARealOrg\" is not a known organisation on this network"

--- B2. RecordAssembly on a component shipped laterally to Tier-1, not the OEM -- expect rejection ---
(setup RegisterComponent + RecordTest AUTH2-NEG-ASM as OEM, then RecordShipment to Org2MSP -- a legitimate lateral shipment to Tier-1, not the OEM -- all committed VALID)
Error: endorsement failure during invoke. response: status:500 message:"recordAssembly rejected for component AUTH2-NEG-ASM: caller Org1MSP is not the current owner of token AUTH2-NEG-ASM (owner is Org2MSP)"

This is the exact scenario the fix targets: the OEM has the correct
*role* to call RecordAssembly (requireCallerIs passes), but does not
*hold* this specific component -- Tier-1 does, following a genuine
lateral shipment. The per-component requireCallerIsOwner check catches
what the role check alone could not.

--- B3. RecordDelivery with an empty dealerID -- expect rejection ---
(setup RegisterComponent + RecordTest + RecordShipment + RecordAssembly AUTH2-NEG-DEL as OEM, all committed VALID)
Error: endorsement failure during invoke. response: status:500 message:"recordDelivery rejected: dealerID is required"

--- B4. RegisterComponent declaring a fabricated co-attesting org -- expect rejection ---
Error: endorsement failure during invoke. response: status:500 message:"declared co-attesting org \"FakeOrgXYZ\" is not a known organisation on this network"

=== DONE: Scenario 10 complete. All four proactive checks reject the
